      "id": "new-hampshire-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/XXV/288/288-1.htm",
      "title": "The legal holidays of New Hampshire (RSA 288:1) that `us-federal-holidays`\ndoes not already close: \"the day on which the biennial election is held\",\nthe Tuesday after the first Monday in November of an even year (the election\nstatute fixing it is not vendored), listed with `once` from the date the\nvendored text was retrieved (October 29, 2026) to the end of 2050. The\nsection's other days are federal holidays, a Sunday one observed the day\nafter (RSA 288:2) as § 6103(b)(1) observes it. Not modeled: a Thanksgiving\nappointed on a day other than the federal one, which no vendored source\nlists."
    }
